join Zanele (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
- Are you all right?
	Hope: Are you all right?
	Zanele: I am thinking about something I did in March and have not told anybody about.
	- Do you want to tell me?
		Hope: Do you want to tell me?
		Zanele: No. Not because I do not trust you — because saying it out loud makes it a thing that might happen.
	Zanele: There is a point where keeping a person close is not the same as helping them. I have known that for a long time. I teach it to parents, sometimes, when they want a child to leave school and work.
	Zanele: It is a different matter when —
	Zanele: It is a different matter.
